    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter today\u2019s slate with a high-floor offensive projection anchored by the top-tier efficiency of **Kyle Tucker** (74.92), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.96), and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.16). **Kyle Tucker** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Brandon Young; despite a minor downgrade for a #7 batting position, his raw talent and platoon advantage drive him to the top of our ranks. Simultaneously, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in an ideal spot against Nick Martinez, where the SP\u2019s high-4.00 xERA and a favorable platoon matchup boost his baseline to elite status. **Drake Baldwin** and **Andy Pages** also stand out as strong plays (70.07 and 71.39, respectively), both capitalizing on soft pitching matchups\u2014Gasser and Young\u2014to deliver substantial value without the hindrance of elite-tier opposing arms.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's bench involved **Jacob Wilson**, who narrowly missed the cut with a score of 51.41. While his park factors are positive, he was ultimately outpaced by the higher offensive efficiency profiles of **Wade Meckler** and **Liam Hicks**, who, despite potential volatility in their batting order slots, offer more favorable platoon alignments against their respective opponents. We continue to monitor the status of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Nolan Schanuel**, and **Jackson Merrill**; as \"Lineup Pending\" designations, their scores are tied to assumed order placements. Should these players shift lower in their respective lineups, our efficiency expectations will need to be adjusted downward. While we remain aggressive, we are mindful of the \"Lineup Pending\" risk\u2014particularly with **Liam Hicks**\u2014as any unexpected benching would force us to rely on deeper bench options like **Nasim Nunez** or **Brayan Rocchio** to maintain our competitive edge in the SB category.",
